  15:     """
  16:     Draw each top-edge color downward, turning horizontally only when it reaches its matching endpoint pixel.
  17: 
  18:     Input structure
  19:     A single contiguous run of non-background pixels lies on the top edge; any other
  20:     foreground pixel has a color from that run and acts as that color's endpoint.
  21: 
  22:     Rule
  23:     For each top-edge source pixel, draw a vertical segment down its column to the
  24:     row of the same-colored endpoint, then draw the horizontal segment to that
  25:     endpoint. If the source color has no separate endpoint, draw the vertical
  26:     segment straight down to the bottom edge.
  27: 
  28:     Key insight
  29:     The top run gives the source column for each color, while each matching
  30:     off-edge pixel gives the row and final column where that color's path turns.
