   7: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   8:     """Stack all colored horizontal segments by increasing length, right-aligned above the solid bottom stripe.
   9: 
  10:     Input structure
  11:     The grid has a dominant background, one full-width non-background stripe on
  12:     the bottom row, and one or more 4-connected monochrome foreground objects
  13:     above it. Each non-stripe object is a one-cell-thick horizontal segment.
  14: 
  15:     Rule
  16:     Clear the segment objects from their original positions. Sort the segments
  17:     by length from shortest to longest, then place them in consecutive rows
  18:     immediately above the bottom stripe, with each segment right-aligned to the
  19:     grid's right edge. Keep the bottom stripe unchanged.
  20: 
  21:     Key insight
  22:     The scattered segments are not moved by their original row or color; their
  23:     lengths define a stack order against the fixed bottom stripe.
